        "text": "The regulatory environment surrounding daos is also uncertain. How different jurisdictions will create the regulatory framework around these new types of organizations remains to be seen. The desirable properties of DAOs, such as decentralization and immutability, also carry performance and security drawbacks. It's not complicated to create a dao. Still, if you ever consider doing so, you should remember that a DAO needs a purpose, a voting mechanism, a governance token, and a healthy community to succeed. Well, we've covered DeFi, smart contracts, DApps, and DAOs in this decentralization course. In the broadest definition, decentralization refers to dispersing functions and power away from a central authority to a distributed network. This enables different parties to work together without having to trust each other.",
